msgid "A bankrupt player leaves the active game. The last solvent player wins."
msgstr ""

msgid "A bidder who collects at least the exact contracted number receives the contract value; otherwise the same value is subtracted. Each defender receives the exact points collected and then rounded to the nearest 5. A rounded result is never used to decide whether the bidder fulfilled the contract."
msgstr ""

#: games/mancala.rb:52
msgid "A board full of seeds"
msgstr ""

#: games/checkers.rb:72
msgid "A capture sequence must be completed"
msgstr "Je nutné dokončit celou sérii braní"

msgid "A capture sequence must be completed is on by default. After a jump, continue capturing with the same piece while a continuation is available. The interface performs the jumps one at a time. With this option off the turn ends after one jump. Prefer a king when equally long captures are available is off by default; when enabled, equally long maximum captures by a king take precedence over those by a man."
msgstr ""

msgid "A chat command such as /d3 attempts a move on that square, using the same rules as Enter."
msgstr "Příkaz v chatu, například /d3, se pokusí provést tah na daném poli podle stejných pravidel jako Enter."

#: games/uno.rb:105
msgid "A colour-changing wild is played in two steps. First it leaves your hand and becomes the table card; then you select a colour. Nobody can intercept between those steps. A configured thinking timer is paused during this colour choice. The next player receives their full turn time once the colour is chosen."
msgstr ""

#: lib/table_activity_repository.rb:231
msgid "A computer takes over %{player}'s place."
msgstr ""

#: games/quiz_party.rb:82
msgid "A correct answer gives one point. A wrong answer or no answer gives zero; there are no negative points. Answering first earns no extra points, provided everyone answers within the time allowed. You can therefore use the available time to think instead of racing to press Enter."
msgstr ""

msgid "A correct answer is worth one point. A wrong or missing answer is worth no points, and there are no negative points."
msgstr ""

msgid "A correct guess earns one point for the describing team. A skip or accepted violation earns one point for the other team, without subtracting another point. An unfinished card at timeout scores zero. Late or simultaneous submissions cannot score the next card; the first accepted decision applies provisionally."
msgstr ""

#: games/taboo_ui.rb:86
msgid "A correct guess gives your team one point. A skipped card or accepted violation gives the other team one point; it does not also subtract a point from yours. An unfinished card at timeout gives neither team a point. If decisions arrive together, the first accepted one applies provisionally to that card. A late key press cannot score a different, newly displayed card."
msgstr ""

msgid "A correct unique answer is worth 10 points, a correct duplicated answer is worth 5 points, and an empty or rejected answer is worth 0 points."
msgstr ""

#: games/reversi.rb:149
msgid "A disc placed here would not enclose any opposing discs."
msgstr "Kámen položený sem by neuzavřel žádné soupeřovy kameny."

#: games/domino.rb:143
msgid "A domino tile has two numbers, one at each end. On your turn, attach one tile to either end of the chain so that touching numbers match. For example, with 2 at the left end and 5 at the right, a 2/6 can go on the left and a 5/1 on the right. The program turns the tile the right way round. Only the two outer ends are playable; you cannot attach tiles in the middle."
msgstr ""

msgid "A double grants another play on any accessible train. Further doubles continue your turn. During your own series you may cover an earlier double while leaving a later one on another train. Remove only the obligation you actually covered. A non-double ends the turn. A double played as your last tile wins immediately, without drawing or covering it."
msgstr ""

msgid "A draw attack always targets the next seat and never rebounds to its author. A player who is already waiting cannot defend against a two, three, attacking king or equivalent joker: the cards are drawn automatically and that resolution consumes one waiting turn."
msgstr ""

#: games/makao.rb:135
msgid "A drawn playable card may be played immediately"
msgstr "Dobranou kartu, kterou lze zahrát, je možné zahrát ihned"

msgid "A finished move advances automatically; there is no required End turn button. Doubles normally give another roll after resolving the field. Three consecutive doubles send you to jail instead of moving for the third roll. Going to jail or going into debt removes the extra roll."
msgstr ""

#: games/makao.rb:79
msgid "A four makes the next player wait. With accumulating fours enabled, another four or a packet of fours passes on a larger waiting penalty. The player who accepts it waits that many turns, including the current one; later waiting turns are skipped automatically. If accumulation is disabled, a four simply skips one turn and cannot be answered by another four."
msgstr ""

msgid "A four requires waiting. With Fours accumulate skipped turns enabled, answer with another four or a packet of fours to pass on the increased number. Whoever accepts waits exactly that many turns, including the current one, and is automatically skipped on later waiting turns. With accumulation off, a four causes one missed turn and cannot be answered with another four."
msgstr ""

msgid "A full column cannot be selected. After a valid move, the turn passes to the other player."
msgstr ""

#: __app.rb:2692 __app.rb:2734
msgid "A game has already started. Opening the current game."
msgstr "Hra již začala. Otevírání probíhající hry."

msgid "A jack does not add points. A four still adds four when it reverses direction. The ace and ten choices are made before playing the card; the program never permits a negative pile."
msgstr ""

#: games/rummy_ui.rb:126
msgid "A joker in your hand cannot be added directly to an existing combination. Use it when making a new combination with at least two natural cards. With manipulations enabled, those cards may include ones you have legally taken from the table. This restriction also matters after recovering a joker: having somewhere to put a normal card does not necessarily give you somewhere to put the joker."
msgstr ""

#: games/monopoly.rb:58
msgid "A journey of buying and collecting rent"
msgstr ""

#: games/checkers.rb:293
msgid "A king has priority for an equally long capture. Choose a king on %{fields}."
msgstr "Při stejně dlouhém braní má přednost dáma. Vyberte dámu na některém z polí: %{fields}."

#: games/domino.rb:145
msgid "A larger set means more copies and more numbers"
msgstr ""

msgid "A later Yahtzee bonus and the Joker rule are independent options. Pair, two pairs and misery are optional extra categories and are enabled by default."
msgstr ""

#: games/scrabble_ui.rb:54
msgid "A letter shared by two new words scores in both. Bonuses work only on the move that first covers them; extending a word later does not activate its old bonuses again. A blank still scores zero on a letter bonus, but can activate a word bonus. Using all seven rack tiles in one move adds 50 points after the word totals have been calculated."
msgstr ""

#: games/tic_tac_toe.rb:33
msgid "A line can run across a row, down a column or along either diagonal. For example, owning the top-left, centre and bottom-right squares wins the game. The game ends as soon as a line is completed, even if other squares are still empty. If the board fills up without a winning line, the result is a draw."
msgstr ""

msgid "A match is played in rounds of three questions. At the start of every round three categories are drawn at random, one player chooses one of them for all three questions, and that choice rotates between the players."
msgstr ""

#: games/monopoly.rb:76
msgid "A mortgage pays you the property's mortgage value, while the property remains yours and stops earning rent. Before mortgaging a street, sell every building in its colour group. To remove the mortgage later, pay the mortgage amount plus 10%, rounded up to a whole money unit. For example, a mortgage of 100 costs 110 to clear. The lists display the actual payment before confirmation."
msgstr ""

msgid "A negative balance ends your current turn, even after doubles. Other players take their normal turns before your next turn begins. Only then do you sell buildings, mortgage or trade to cover the deficit. Roll remains the main action but reports the missing amount instead of rolling until the balance is no longer negative. A charge outside your turn does not interrupt someone else's move."
msgstr ""

msgid "A negative balance ends your current turn, including any extra roll. Other players take their turns before you manage your debt on your next turn. Until the debt is paid, Roll reports the missing amount. A debt charged outside your turn does not interrupt the current player."
msgstr ""

#: games/chess.rb:56
msgid "A pawn moves forward towards the opponent's starting side. It advances one square into an empty square. From its starting row it may instead advance two, provided both squares are empty. It captures differently: one square diagonally forward. A pawn cannot move backwards or capture straight ahead."
msgstr ""

msgid "A pawn moves one empty field forward, toward the opponent's starting side. From its starting rank it may move two fields if both are empty. It captures one field diagonally forward, never straight ahead. On reaching the last rank it must become a queen, rook, bishop or knight, chosen from a list."
msgstr ""

#: games/chess.rb:57
msgid "A pawn reaching the farthest row is promoted. Choose a queen, rook, bishop or knight from the list. This choice is not limited to pieces that have already been captured: you can have two queens."
msgstr ""

#: games/categories.rb:211
msgid "A permanent judge requires at least two participants."
msgstr "Hra se stálým rozhodčím vyžaduje alespoň dva účastníky."

#: games/categories.rb:90
msgid "A person judges the answers"
msgstr ""

#: games/krowa_support/presentation.rb:24
msgid "A person who surrenders a Race immediately learns the solution without revealing it to players who are still racing."
msgstr ""

#: games/rummy_ui.rb:134
msgid "A played joker scores as the card it represents; a joker left in the hand is worth 20. For example, with rounding, a run of 3, 4 and joker scores 15 because it represents 3-4-5. The same card values are used when checking your first meld and counting unfinished hands."
msgstr ""

msgid "A player can win only the contributions matched by their investment. Larger investments create side pots contested by their contributors who have not folded. Equal best hands split a pot. Combinations from weakest to strongest are high card, pair, two pairs, three of a kind, straight, flush, full house, four of a kind and straight flush. Aces can be low in A-2-3-4-5; suits do not break equal hands. Ranks within the combination, then kickers, decide ties."
msgstr ""

msgid "A player may remain active with zero tokens. Elimination occurs only when the player later owes more tokens than are available. When one active player remains, that player wins the game."
msgstr ""

msgid "A player who cannot pay the bid, or chooses not to, is penalised, and the card is auctioned again without her. Under the medieval bluff she discards one card at random; under the full penalty the other players each take a card at random from her hand."
msgstr ""

#: games/war.rb:43
msgid "A player who has no cards left after a battle is out of the game. The last player with cards wins."
msgstr ""

msgid "A player who takes exactly zero unrounded points in 3 played deals is penalized 120 points. A result such as 2 points that merely rounds to zero does not count, and zero-point deals do not accumulate while that player is on the barrel."
msgstr ""

msgid "A player wins when the opponent has no pieces or no legal move. Three repetitions or 80 moves without a capture or promotion are a draw."
msgstr ""

#: games/war.rb:39
msgid "A player with only one card left plays it face up without a hidden card. A player with no cards cannot continue the war; if only one participant can continue, they take the table. If nobody can continue, the cards stay on the table and go to the winner of the next battle."
msgstr ""

#: games/rummy_ui.rb:128
msgid "A recovered joker is a borrowed table card. Play it back onto the table before ending your turn to avoid a 300-point penalty. You may keep it instead and accept that penalty. The same rule applies to other borrowed cards in the manipulation variant. Discarding a borrowed card does not count as playing it back."
msgstr ""

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:204
msgid "A removed bot no longer remains in the waiting table's team list after a previous match was stopped."
msgstr "Odebraný bot už po zastavení předchozího zápasu nezůstává na seznamu týmů čekajícího stolu."

#: games/ludo.rb:71
msgid "A roll gives one pawn a move"
msgstr ""

msgid "A roll of 1 ends the turn immediately. After any other roll, you may choose again between rolling and banking. Players take turns in seating order, starting with the first person at the table."
msgstr ""

#: games/quiz_party.rb:84
msgid "A round consists of three questions. At its start, the game draws three available categories and one participant chooses which will be used for all three questions. The right to choose moves between players in successive rounds. Category choices include their question counts so you can see how much material they contain."
msgstr ""

msgid "A round ends when a player uses the last card. Players reaching the cumulative score limit are eliminated and become observers. The last remaining player wins."
msgstr ""

#: games/rummy_ui.rb:116
msgid "A run contains at least three consecutive cards of the same suit, placed in ascending order. For example, 6, 7 and 8 of hearts is a run; three sevens of different suits are not. An ace may come before 2 or after king, so A-2-3 and Q-K-A are valid, but K-A-2 is not. A set contains three or four cards of the same rank in different suits."
msgstr ""

#: games/farkle.rb:49
msgid "A run of five consecutive values, 1 to 5 or 2 to 6, gives 100. A run from 1 to 6 gives 200. Three pairs of different values give 150. Two different triples give 250, as do four equal dice together with a pair of another value. That last combination uses six dice; it is not the five-dice full house from Yahtzee."
msgstr ""

msgid "A score from 120 points below the target up to one point below it is placed on the barrel and set to exactly 120 below the target. A player on the barrel must successfully complete a contract of at least 120 within the next 3 deals. Defender points do not count on the barrel. Failing such a contract removes its normal value and leaves the barrel; running out of the 3 deals costs 120 points and also leaves the barrel."
msgstr ""

msgid "A selection must use every chosen die in a scoring group; stray twos, threes, fours or sixes cannot be attached for free. Several scoring groups from the same roll can be combined. When more than one interpretation uses the selected dice, the program awards the highest valid score. Previously kept dice do not help form a group in a later roll."
msgstr ""

#: games/yahtzee.rb:73
msgid "A sheet takes 13 turns per player, or 16 with the extra rows. Number of matches chooses how many complete sheets everyone plays, from 1 to 10, normally 1. A new sheet starts empty. Scores from all sheets are added, and the highest final total wins; equal highest totals mean a tied result."
msgstr ""

#: games/yahtzee.rb:57
msgid "A sheet to fill, not a score to chase forever"
msgstr ""

msgid "A shield protects the whole goal for ten seconds of play. It returns a missed ball straight ahead without being used up. Winning another shield renews its time to ten seconds. An invisible ball is silent until a paddle returns it or a goal is scored. A shield bounce does not reveal it. Activation and shield expiry have distinct sounds; E reports the current effects."
msgstr ""

#: games/axel_pong.rb:270
msgid "A shield protects the whole goal for ten seconds of play. It returns a missed ball straight ahead without being used up. Winning another shield renews its time to ten seconds. An invisible ball is silent until a paddle returns it or a goal is scored. A shield bounce does not reveal it. Activation and shield expiry have distinct sounds; E reports the current effects. The remaining shield time is preserved between points and does not run down while waiting for a serve."
msgstr ""

#: games/battleship.rb:55
msgid "A ship must form one straight horizontal or vertical line, without gaps. It cannot bend, run diagonally, overlap another ship or go outside the board. By default, ships must not touch, even at a corner. Enabling Ships may touch removes that spacing restriction, but never allows two ships on the same square."
msgstr ""

#: games/battleship.rb:322 games/battleship.rb:669
msgid "A ship must lie in one row or one column."
msgstr "Loď musí ležet v jednom řádku nebo jednom sloupci."

msgid "A single 5 scores 5 points and a single 1 scores 10. Three 1s score 75; three of any other face score ten times that face. Four of a kind score 110 to 160, five of a kind 320 to 420, and six of a kind 625 to 750."
msgstr ""

#: games/farkle.rb:47
msgid "A single one is worth 10 points; a single five is worth 5. Other single dice do not score. Three ones give 75. Three twos, threes, fours, fives or sixes give 20, 30, 40, 50 or 60 respectively."
msgstr ""

msgid "A single one scores 10 and a single five scores 5. Three ones score 75; triples of 2, 3, 4, 5 and 6 score 20, 30, 40, 50 and 60 respectively. Four equal dice score 100 plus ten times their face (110–160). Five equal dice score 300 plus twenty times their face (320–420). Six equal dice score 600 plus twenty-five times their face (625–750)."
msgstr ""

#: games/poker.rb:95
msgid "A small all-in can win only the money matched by that player's contribution. Extra investments form side pots for the other eligible players. For example, with contributions of 50, 100 and 100, the first 150 can be won by all three; the remaining 100 is contested only by the last two. Each pot is settled separately. Any odd chips in a split go clockwise to tied winners, starting to the left of the dealer."
msgstr ""

#: games/tic_tac_toe.rb:30
msgid "A small board, three marks to win"
msgstr ""

msgid "A small straight scores 100, a large straight 200, three pairs 150, and a full house or two sets of three of a kind score 250. The program lists every legal scoring interpretation and automatically uses the points belonging to the selected combination."
msgstr ""

#: games/tysiac.rb:93
msgid "A successful bidder receives exactly the contract value, not all the points collected. A failed bidder loses the contract value. Defenders add their collected points rounded to the nearest five. The bidder's success is checked before rounding: 118 points do not fulfil a contract of 120."
msgstr ""

#: games/audio_ball.rb:195
msgid "A successful defence leaves you holding the ball; it does not return it automatically. Press Right arrow or A to prepare your shot, then make a new press of one of the three shot keys to attack. You may choose any shot type. Prepare in the same way before every serve, including the first serve of the match. Keeping a shot key held down through preparation will not launch the ball."
msgstr ""

msgid "A successful nil, a bid of zero with no tricks won, gives 100 points. A failed nil costs 100 points, and its tricks become overtricks in standard play. In a team, a nil is scored separately and its tricks do not help the partner's ordinary contract."
msgstr ""

#: games/taboo_ui.rb:89
msgid "A technical restart is for a disrupted turn, not for correcting just one card. It cancels all points from that turn and gives the same describer a new turn with new cards. Cards already exposed remain used. The shuffled deck avoids repeats until it runs out and avoids an immediate repeat when reshuffling. You may save between turns after the review has been approved."
msgstr ""

msgid "A tied lead can be a shared victory or trigger extra play, the default. Only the tied leaders keep competing. With rotating judging, someone outside that group judges if available; if everyone is tied, judging still rotates through a complete cycle. A permanent judge remains the judge. Extra play continues until the tie is broken; lower-scoring players do not rejoin the race."
msgstr ""

#: games/categories.rb:102
msgid "A tied lead can give a shared victory or require extra play, the default. In extra play only the tied leaders remain in contention. An outside participant judges if possible; if everyone is tied, judging continues over complete cycles. A permanent judge keeps that role. Further play continues until the tied lead is resolved. This game does not support saving a partly completed match."
msgstr ""

#: games/domino.rb:159
msgid "A time limit for each turn"
msgstr ""

msgid "A trade can include several properties and cash on either side. E first opens the player list. Enter chooses the partner and announces that you are preparing an offer; it does not send an empty offer. The next form contains both cash amounts, one arrow-key list of your properties, one arrow-key list of the other player's properties and Send proposal. Tab moves between those whole sections. Escape returns from the form to the player list. The recipient can accept or reject; nothing transfers before acceptance. Mortgaged properties and streets in a built-up group cannot be traded. The proposal must remain affordable and valid. Computers consider both sides' gains and avoid repeatedly sending the same rejected proposal."
msgstr ""

msgid "A trade can include several properties and cash on either side. Select the other player, what you offer and what you request. The recipient can accept or reject; nothing transfers before acceptance. Mortgaged properties and streets in a built-up group cannot be traded. The proposal must remain affordable and valid. Computers consider both sides' gains and avoid repeatedly sending the same rejected proposal."
msgstr ""

#: games/monopoly.rb:78
msgid "A trade may combine properties and cash from either side. E opens the players; Enter chooses a partner and announces that you are preparing an offer. It does not send an empty offer. In the form, enter the two cash amounts and choose properties from the two checkbox lists. Arrows move within a property list, while Tab moves between the form's sections. Send proposal submits the complete offer; Escape returns to the player list."
msgstr ""

#: games/mexican_train.rb:110
msgid "A train is simply a chain of matching dominoes. Everyone has a personal train, initially closed to other players, and there is one shared Mexican train, always open. You may play on your own train, the Mexican train or another player's open train. Match the number at its outer end; an empty train still ends at the station's number. The first starter is chosen at random, and the starting seat then rotates between rounds."
msgstr ""

#: games/spades.rb:212
msgid "A trick is one card played by each player in turn. One player wins those cards and starts the next trick. In Spades, you first promise how many tricks you will win. Taking too few is expensive, but taking far too many can hurt as well. Spades are always trumps: they beat cards of the other suits."
msgstr ""

msgid "A turn"
msgstr ""

msgid "A turn may play one card or a packet of equal ranks. At least one card in the packet must legally match the table; the whole packet is recorded as one action."
msgstr ""

msgid "A turn may play one card or a packet of equal ranks. The first selected card must legally match the table; the whole packet is recorded as one action."
msgstr ""

#: games/makao.rb:77
msgid "A two adds two cards to the next player's penalty, and a three adds three. Instead of paying, the attacked player can answer with a permitted attacking card. The debt then passes on and grows. With mixed twos and threes enabled, a two answered by a three makes five cards. With it disabled, the responding rank must match the attack."
msgstr ""

#: games/ninety_nine.rb:84
msgid "A two normally doubles the total. However, if the total is even and greater than 49, it halves it instead: 60 becomes 30. A jack adds 10 and skips the next player. With two players, this gives its author another turn. A four still adds four, but also reverses direction when at least three players remain."
msgstr ""

msgid "A two normally doubles the total. However, if the total is even and greater than 49, it halves it instead: 60 becomes 30. A jack adds nothing and skips the next player. With two players, this gives its author another turn. A four still adds four, but also reverses direction when at least three players remain."
msgstr ""

msgid "A unique answer is worth 10 points. A partially correct answer or an accepted identical group is worth 5 points per author. An empty or rejected answer is worth 0 points."
msgstr ""

msgid "A unique answer is worth 2 points. A partially correct answer or an accepted identical group is worth 1 point per author. An empty or rejected answer is worth 0 points."
msgstr ""

#: games/categories.rb:92
msgid "A unique correct answer is worth 2 points. An accepted repeated answer gives each author 1 point, as does an answer judged partially correct. An incorrect or empty answer gives zero. Everyone can see the grades and authors. Once every answer group has been assessed, the judge finishes the review and the round's points are added to the scores."
msgstr ""

msgid "A wild card that requires a colour is placed on the discard pile first, and choosing its colour is a separate visible action. Once the wild has been played, nobody can intercept before its owner chooses the colour. Thinking time is paused during this choice; the next player's full time starts only after the colour has been selected."
msgstr ""

#: games/four_in_a_row.rb:34
msgid "A winning line may be horizontal, vertical or diagonal. All its pieces must touch: a gap or an opponent's piece breaks the line. Completing a line ends the game immediately. If all 42 squares fill up without a winner, the game is drawn."
msgstr ""

#: games/scrabble.rb:125
msgid "A word must contain at least two letters."
msgstr "Slovo musí obsahovat alespoň dvě písmena."

#: games/taboo_ui.rb:83
msgid "A wrong guess is harmless: teammates may keep trying. People decide whether an answer is close enough or a different grammatical form should count. Before playing, agree on a consistent approach to such answers. The app does not recognise spoken words and cannot decide a disputed clue for you."
msgstr ""

#: games/monopoly.rb:123
msgid "A: accept an incoming offer."
msgstr "A: přijměte příchozí nabídku."

#: games/poker.rb:109
msgid "A: go all-in."
msgstr "A: vsaďte vše."

#: games/audio_ball.rb:226 lib/game_surfaces/audio_ball_surface.rb:111
msgid "A: prepare a shot while holding the ball before a serve or after a defence."
msgstr "A: připravte úder, když držíte míč před podáním nebo po obraně."

msgid "A: prepare to serve or to hit after defending."
msgstr "A: připravte se na podání nebo na úder po obraně."

#: games/axel_pong.rb:249
msgid "About this adaptation"
msgstr ""

#: __app.rb:1738 __app.rb:1938 __app.rb:2790
msgid "Accept"
msgstr "Přijmout"

#: __app.rb:2121 lib/game_room_screens.rb:120 lib/game_room_widget.rb:139 lib/game_room_widget.rb:145
msgid "Accept invitation"
msgstr "Přijmout pozvání"

#: games/monopoly.rb:1428
msgid "Accept the proposed trade"
msgstr "Přijmout navrženou výměnu"

#: games/makao.rb:408
msgid "Accept waiting for %{count} turn"
msgid_plural "Accept waiting for %{count} turns"
msgstr[0] "Přijmout vynechání %{count} tahu"
msgstr[1] "Přijmout vynechání %{count} tahů"
msgstr[2] "Přijmout vynechání %{count} tahů"

msgid "Accept waiting for %{count} turns"
msgstr "Přijmout čekání na tento počet tahů: %{count}"

#: __app.rb:2006 __app.rb:2027
msgid "Accepting invitation"
msgstr "Přijímání pozvánky"

#: games/makao.rb:127
msgid "Ace changes suit"
msgstr "Eso mění barvu"

msgid "Ace changes suit lets an ace be played on any ordinary table card and opens the choice of a suit. It does not cancel a pending draw or waiting penalty. If disabled, aces only match normally. Jack requests a rank from 5 to 10 makes a played jack request one of those ranks from the next player. With it off, jacks are ordinary cards."
msgstr ""

#: games/makao.rb:82
msgid "Ace changes suit lets you start an ordinary move with an ace regardless of the table card and choose a suit. It is not a way out of a pending drawing or waiting penalty. With the option off, an ace follows the ordinary matching rule."
msgstr ""

#: games/checkers.rb:106
msgid "Across the dark squares"
msgstr ""

msgid "Actions"
msgstr "Akce"

#: games/cat_head_tail.rb:170 games/farkle.rb:366
msgid "Actions. Use the arrow keys and press Enter"
msgstr "Akce. Vyberte šipkami a stiskněte Enter"

#: games/cat_head_tail.rb:170
msgctxt "cat_head_tail"
msgid "Actions. Use the arrow keys and press Enter"
msgstr "Akce. Vyberte šipkami a stiskněte Enter"

msgid "Activate Roll, then choose a pawn on the board and press Enter, followed by its marked destination. Press P for your pawn positions, Shift+P for the opponents' pawn positions, T for the turn and Ctrl+F1 for these rules."
msgstr "Aktivujte Hodit, poté vyberte figurku na hrací desce a stiskněte Enter. Následně stejným způsobem vyberte její označené cílové pole. Klávesa P přečte pozice vašich figurek, Shift+P pozice figurek soupeřů, T oznámí, kdo je na tahu, a Ctrl+F1 otevře tato pravidla."

msgid "Activate Roll, then choose a pawn on the board and press Enter, followed by its marked destination. Press T to hear whose turn it is and Ctrl+F1 for these rules."
msgstr "Aktivujte tlačítko Hodit, poté vyberte figurku na hrací desce a stiskněte Enter. Následně vyberte její označené cílové pole. Klávesou T zjistíte, kdo je na tahu, a klávesovou zkratkou Ctrl+F1 otevřete tato pravidla."

#: games/ninety_nine.rb:1065
msgid "Add 1"
msgstr "Přičíst 1"

#: games/ninety_nine.rb:1063
msgid "Add 10"
msgstr "Přičíst 10"

#: games/ninety_nine.rb:1066
msgid "Add 11"
msgstr "Přičíst 11"

#: lib/participant_menu.rb:19
msgid "Add a computer"
msgstr "Přidat počítačového hráče"

#: __app.rb:1734
msgid "Add a new computer in this place"
msgstr ""

#: games/krowa_support/presentation.rb:58
msgid "Add noun to dictionary and check"
msgstr "Přidat podstatné jméno do slovníku a zkontrolovat"

#: lib/table_activity_repository.rb:182
msgid "Added %{bot} at %{owner}'s table for %{game}."
msgstr "Ke stolu hostitele %{owner} pro hru %{game} byl přidán bot %{bot}."

#: lib/table_activity_repository.rb:197
msgid "Added %{bot}."
msgstr "Přidán %{bot}."

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:275
msgid "Added 3-5-8 by Guliwer777: a card game for three players, with trick-taking, contract selection and card exchanges between deals. You can also play against bots."
msgstr ""

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:239
msgid "Added Audio Ball by budyn1211, known on ELTEN as balteam: an audio game for two players, against another person or a bot. Recognize three shot sounds, choose the matching defence and prepare your return. Sets are played to seven points with a two-point lead; choose one, two or three sets to win."
msgstr ""

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:185
msgid "Added Axel Pong Doubles by budyn1211: two teams of two players, with alternating returns and shared scores. Spectators can use 1–4 to choose a player's perspective. Partners have distinguishable step and return sounds."
msgstr "Přidána hra Axel Pong Doubles od budyn1211: dva týmy po dvou hráčích, střídání při odehrávání míče a společné skóre. Diváci mohou pomocí 1–4 zvolit pohled hráče. Spoluhráče lze rozlišit podle zvuků kroků a úderů."

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:170
msgid "Added Axel Pong, an audio ping-pong game for two people or a player and a bot, with Classic and Arcade Classic modes and six difficulty levels. Play with the keyboard or mouse. Ctrl+P at the table opens personal settings for automatic return and sound volumes, also available in Settings > Axel Pong."
msgstr "Přidán Axel Pong, zvukový stolní tenis pro dva hráče nebo hráče a bota, s režimy Classic a Arcade Classic a šesti úrovněmi obtížnosti. Hrát můžete klávesnicí nebo myší. Ctrl+P u stolu otevře osobní nastavení automatického vracení míčku a hlasitostí, dostupné také přes Nastavení > Axel Pong."

msgid "Added Axel Pong: follow the ball by sound, move your paddle and return it to your opponent. Play against another person or a bot, with six difficulty levels and a target of 7, 11 or 21 points, won by a two-point lead. Choose Classic or Arcade Classic, which adds temporary shields and an invisible ball."
msgstr "Přidána hra Axel Pong: sledujte míček podle zvuku, pohybujte pálkou a odrážejte jej k soupeři. Hrajte proti jiné osobě nebo botovi se šesti úrovněmi obtížnosti a cílem 7, 11 nebo 21 bodů; k vítězství je nutný náskok dvou bodů. Vyberte si Classic nebo Arcade Classic, který přidává dočasné štíty a neviditelný míček."

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:141
msgid "Added Battleship by Dawid Pieper: two fleets, manual placement, a computer opponent, spectator boards and a final fleet check. Saving this game for later is not yet available."
msgstr "Přidána hra Lodě od Dawida Piepera: dvě flotily, ruční rozmístění, počítačový soupeř, desky pro diváky a závěrečná kontrola flotil. Uložení této hry na později zatím není k dispozici."

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:202
msgid "Added Cat, head, tail by TD Programs: a dice game for 2–8 players. Roll an eight-sided die and decide when to bank your points. Includes bots and Polish and English rules."
msgstr "Přidána hra Kočka, hlava, ocas od TD Programs: kostková hra pro 2–8 hráčů. Házejte osmistěnnou kostkou a rozhodujte se, kdy uložit své body. Obsahuje boty a pravidla v polštině a angličtině."

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:276
msgid "Added Czech and Spanish interface translations by balteam. Choose the language in Settings > General. These translations do not include game rules. Tysiac is now called 1000 card game in English."
msgstr ""

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:147
msgid "Added Krowa by paulinux: guess Polish words in the daily puzzle, solo play, Race or cooperative Word Tower, with a personal gallery and optional leaderboards."
msgstr "Přidána hra Krowa od paulinux: hádejte polská slova v denní hádance, samostatné hře, režimu Závod nebo kooperativním režimu Věž slov, s vlastní galerií a volitelnými žebříčky."

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:142
msgid "Added Mancala by Dawid Pieper, with Oware, Ayoayo and Kalah variants and three computer strengths. Both new games include clear Polish and English rules, keyboard help and move sounds."
msgstr "Byla přidána hra Mancala od Dawida Piepera s variantami Oware, Ayoayo a Kalah a třemi úrovněmi počítačového soupeře. Obě nové hry obsahují srozumitelná pravidla v polštině a angličtině, nápovědu ke klávesám a zvuky tahů."

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:274
msgid "Added War and Scientific War by balteam, for two to eight players, with bots. War compares cards from a face-down deck; Scientific War lets you choose your cards and use their special powers."
msgstr ""

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:177
msgid "Added a Draw another word button to Krowa's Random word variant. It reveals the previous word and resets attempts without recording a win."
msgstr "Do varianty Náhodné slovo ve hře Krowa bylo přidáno tlačítko Vylosovat jiné slovo. Odhalí předchozí slovo a vynuluje pokusy, aniž by se započítalo vítězství."

msgid "Added a test adaptation of Axel Pong: follow the ball by sound, move your paddle and return it to your opponent. Play against another person or a bot, with six difficulty levels and a target of 7, 11 or 21 points, won by a two-point lead."
msgstr "Byla přidána zkušební adaptace hry Axel Pong: sledujte míček podle zvuku, pohybujte pálkou a odrážejte jej k soupeři. Můžete hrát proti člověku nebo botovi, vybrat si ze šesti úrovní obtížnosti a hrát do 7, 11 nebo 21 bodů s požadovaným náskokem dvou bodů."

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:265
msgid "Added missing Polish messages, including the notice that Daily Krowa requires a private table."
msgstr ""

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:128
msgid "Added sounds for banking points in Farkle, reaching exactly 33 or 66 in 99, and declaring a marriage in Tysiac."
msgstr "Byly přidány zvuky pro uložení bodů ve Farkle, dosažení přesně 33 nebo 66 ve hře 99 a oznámení hlášky ve hře Tisíc."

#: __app.rb:1636
msgid "Adding computer"
msgstr "Přidávání počítačového hráče"

#: games/yahtzee.rb:289
msgid "Additional Yahtzee bonuses: %{points}."
msgstr "Bonusy za další Yahtzee: %{points}."

msgid "Adnan Menderes Hava alani"
msgstr "Letiště Adnana Menderese"

msgid "Advance to Start and collect %{amount}."
msgstr "Přejděte na Start a získejte %{amount}."

#: games/uno.rb:147
msgid "Advanced responses"
msgstr "Pokročilé reakce"

#: games/uno.rb:107
msgid "Advanced responses requires ordinary responses and is off by default. Skip or Wild passes the debt onwards; Reverse sends it in the other direction. In No Mercy, Discard All and Skip Everyone instead cancel a pending numerical drawing penalty."
msgstr ""

msgid "Aerodrom Car Konstantin - Niš"
msgstr "Letiště Konstantina Velikého – Niš"

msgid "Aerodrom Nikola Tesla - Beograd"
msgstr "Letiště Nikoly Tesly v Bělehradě"

msgid "Aeroportul Internaţional Henri Coandă"
msgstr "Mezinárodní letiště Henriho Coandy"

msgid "After a Pong point, key presses from the break no longer serve the next ball by themselves. Fixed an error when a new rally had not arrived yet, and clarified the first-serve announcements. Two human players wait until both sides are ready; a bot match does not use that initial countdown."
msgstr "Po získání bodu v Pongu již stisky kláves během přestávky samy nepodají další míček. Opravena chyba, která nastávala, když ještě nedorazila nová výměna, a upřesněna oznámení prvního podání. Dva lidští hráči čekají, dokud nejsou připraveny obě strany; zápas s botem toto úvodní odpočítávání nepoužívá."

#: games/poker.rb:23
msgid "After a number of hands"
msgstr "Po určitém počtu rozdání"

#: games/poker.rb:24
msgid "After a number of minutes"
msgstr "Po určitém počtu minut"

#: games/audio_ball.rb:211
msgid "After a point, the game plays an announcement and reads the score: yours first, then your opponent's. When needed, speech synthesis replaces the recorded score announcement. Observers hear the scores in the order of players at the table."
msgstr ""

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:22
msgid "After a second review, 284 well-supported Quiz Party questions were restored without bringing back ambiguous questions."
msgstr "Po druhé kontrole bylo obnoveno 284 otázek Quiz Party s dobře doloženými odpověďmi, aniž by se vrátily nejednoznačné otázky."

#: games/krowa_support/presentation.rb:26
msgid "After a word ends, the solution is revealed. The Word definition button opens its SJP description; a missing description also remains readable."
msgstr ""

#: games/three_five_eight.rb:82
msgid "After any exchanges, the chooser reveals the four-card kitty, adds it to their hand and discards four cards face down. The chooser leads the first trick. The winner of every trick leads the next one."
msgstr ""

msgid "After completing the shared track, each player enters a private six-field home lane. Reaching its end places the pawn at the finish, where it no longer moves."
msgstr ""

msgid "After defending, you hold the ball. Press Right arrow or A to prepare, then press one of the three shot keys to hit. The server must also prepare before serving. A defence only catches the ball: it does not automatically send it back. An attack does not select the lane for a later incoming ball. Keep focus on the Audio Ball playfield when using these controls. Each new attack needs a fresh press; a selected defensive lane or a key still held after preparation does not hit automatically."
msgstr ""

msgid "After defending, you hold the ball. Press Right arrow or A to prepare, then press one of the three shot keys to hit. The server must also prepare before serving. A defence only catches the ball: it does not automatically send it back. Keep focus on the Audio Ball playfield when using these controls."
msgstr ""

msgid "After defending, you hold the ball. Press Right arrow or A to prepare, then press one of the three shot keys to hit. The server must also prepare before serving. A defence only catches the ball: it does not automatically send it back. Keep focus on the Audio Ball playfield when using these controls. Each new attack needs a fresh press; keeping the defense key held after preparation does not hit automatically."
msgstr ""

msgid "After defending, you hold the ball. Press Right arrow or A to prepare, then press one of the three shot keys to hit. The server must also prepare before serving. A defence only catches the ball: it does not automatically send it back. The shot key also selects your lane for the next defence. Keep focus on the Audio Ball playfield when using these controls. Each new attack needs a fresh press; a selected lane or a key still held after preparation does not hit automatically."
msgstr ""

msgid "After drawing a penalty, your turn also ends if you have no playable card. If skipping after a penalty is enabled, the turn always ends."
msgstr ""

msgid "After each turn, everyone may inspect the used cards. The table master can change a card to guessed, skipped, violation or no points, after discussing disputes. Corrections remain in the history. The master must approve the review before the next turn. Approved scores cannot be edited. A technical restart cancels the whole turn's points and repeats the same describing player with new cards; previously revealed cards stay used."
msgstr ""

msgid "After every round the scores are updated and another deal begins automatically while no unique leader has reached the selected limit. Once there is such a leader, that player or team wins the game."
msgstr ""

msgid "After every selected match is complete, the player with the highest combined score wins."
msgstr ""

#: games/quiz_party.rb:85
msgid "After everyone answers or time expires, the game reveals the answers and awards points, then prepares the next question. Preparing a question is not another answer choice: wait for the new question to appear. Once all three have been settled, the round summary is available and the next category selection begins unless the match has ended."
msgstr ""

#: games/mancala.rb:68
msgid "After gathering the remaining seeds, compare the stores. More seeds wins and equal stores mean a draw. Unlike Oware, Ayoayo does not stop merely because someone has passed half of the total."
msgstr ""

msgid "After giving the cards, the taker may raise the contract within the legal limit based on the marriages still in hand. Playing the first card accepts the current contract without another mandatory bidding step."
msgstr ""

msgid "After keeping a combination, choose either Roll N dice or, once the required minimum has been reached, Bank X points. Rolling continues the same turn with the remaining dice; banking makes the turn points permanent and passes play to the next player."
msgstr ""

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:25
msgid "After playing Wild or Wild Draw Four in UNO, colours are offered in the order yellow, red, blue, green."
msgstr "Po zahrání karty Změna barvy nebo Změna barvy a dobrat čtyři v UNO jsou barvy nabízeny v pořadí žlutá, červená, modrá, zelená."

msgid "After seeing the talon and before giving away a card, the bidder may surrender unless already on the barrel. The bidder receives zero and each defender receives at least 60 points, or half the contract when that is higher, rounded upward to a multiple of 5. The first 2 surrenders are free; every third surrender costs the bidder 120 points."
msgstr ""

#: games/tysiac.rb:100
msgid "After seeing the talon but before giving away or setting aside the first card, the bidder may surrender, unless on the barrel. Each defender receives at least 60, or half the contract if that is higher, rounded upwards to five. With two players there is only one defender, receiving the same award. No last-trick award applies to a surrendered deal. The bidder normally receives zero. Every third surrender additionally costs the bidder 120 points."
msgstr ""

msgid "After seeing the talon but before giving away the first card, the bidder may surrender, unless on the barrel. Each defender receives at least 60, or half the contract if that is higher, rounded upwards to five. The bidder normally receives zero. Every third surrender additionally costs the bidder 120 points."
msgstr ""

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:145
msgid "After selecting a game to create a table, focus starts on the opening instructions again. Tab then moves to Private table and the game settings."
msgstr "Po výběru hry při vytváření stolu se fokus opět přesune na úvodní pokyny. Tab pak přejde na volbu Soukromý stůl a nastavení hry."

#: games/three_five_eight.rb:93
msgid "After the eighteenth deal, the player with the highest total score wins. Equal highest totals produce a shared draw."
msgstr ""

#: games/tysiac.rb:90
msgid "After the first trick, a player leading a trick may declare a marriage by playing its king or queen while still holding the matching partner. The declared suit becomes trump immediately. Hearts add 100 points, diamonds 80, clubs 60 and spades 40. A later marriage changes trump again. Simply owning the pair, or playing it without the declaration, does not award that bonus."
msgstr ""

#: games/biblios.rb:71
msgid "After the last auction is settled, total each player's cards in every category. The highest total wins that category's die. A tied total is decided by the card letter closest to A in that category. A category nobody holds awards nothing. Add the faces of the dice you won to obtain your victory points; card values themselves are not added again."
msgstr ""

#: games/audio_ball.rb:193
msgid "After the opponent hits, listen to the ball and press the matching defence key once. You may press it as soon as you recognise the sound, then release it. That choice remains active for this incoming ball, and you catch it automatically within the final two steps of the court. You do not need to time another press at contact. If you choose the wrong direction, you can correct it before the ball passes you; the last direction you choose is the one that counts."
msgstr ""

msgid "After the shared track a pawn enters its own six-field home lane; opponents cannot enter that lane. The last field is the finish. A pawn at the finish no longer moves and is not offered as a playable pawn."
msgstr ""

msgid "After the turn ends, other players must cover the most recently left unfinished double first, even on a normally closed train. They cannot play elsewhere until it is covered. Uncovered older doubles then remain for the following players, in reverse order. Failure to answer requires one draw, then opening your own train and passing if no answer exists. The obligation stays on the table."
msgstr ""

#: games/taboo_ui.rb:88
msgid "After time expires, everyone may inspect the cards used in that turn. Discuss disputed decisions, then the table master can change a result to guessed, skipped, violation or no points. Changes appear in the history. The master must approve the review before play continues; approved turns cannot be edited later."
msgstr ""

#: games/biblios.rb:59
msgid "After you finish distributing, the other players each choose one public card, starting with the next seat. In a four-player game, you therefore keep one, reserve one for auction and let the other three players choose from the three public cards. Then the next player distributes gifts. Continue until the gift deck is exhausted."
msgstr ""

msgid "After your first meld you can replace a table joker with its actual natural card from your hand. No separate Recover joker menu item is needed. In a three-card set with a joker and two suits, first add a third natural suit; only the fourth missing suit then recovers the joker. A bare joker cannot be appended to an existing meld."
msgstr ""

#: games/rummy_ui.rb:127
msgid "After your first meld, you can recover a table joker by playing the natural card needed in its place. This is a use of the replacement card, not a separate command on the joker. In a three-card set with two natural suits and a joker, first add a third natural suit; the remaining fourth suit can then replace the joker. You cannot simply pull out a joker and leave an invalid combination behind."
msgstr ""

msgid "Agra Station"
msgstr "Nádraží v Ágře"

#: lib/game_history_navigation.rb:129
msgid "All"
msgstr "Vše"

#: lib/game_room_ui.rb:24
msgid "All Game Room sounds"
msgstr "Všechny zvuky Game Room"

#: games/uno.rb:798
msgid "All active players pass their hands to the next player in seating order."
msgstr "Všichni aktivní hráči předají své karty dalšímu hráči podle pořadí u stolu."

#: games/uno.rb:798
msgid "All active players pass their hands to the previous player in seating order."
msgstr "Všichni aktivní hráči předají své karty předchozímu hráči podle pořadí u stolu."

msgid "All active players passed their hands on."
msgstr "Všichni aktivní hráči předali své karty dál."

#: games/makao.rb:479
msgid "All cards in a packet must have the same value."
msgstr "Všechny karty ve skupině musí mít stejnou hodnotu."

msgid "All history"
msgstr "Celá historie"

#: games/poker.rb:1203
msgid "All in; %{amount}"
msgstr "Vše do hry; %{amount}"

msgid "All options appear in one table form. Length applies to Random word and Race, while scoring applies only to Race. Daily Krowa and Word Tower ignore those fields."
msgstr ""

#: games/ludo.rb:266
msgid "All pawns"
msgstr "Všechny figurky"

#: games/farkle.rb:536
msgid "All six dice scored; hot dice."
msgstr "Všech šest kostek bodovalo; horké kostky."

#: lib/game_statistics_periods.rb:43
msgid "All time"
msgstr ""

msgid "All-in commits your remaining chips if the betting structure permits it. It does not itself end the game or automatically win the hand. Players with chips still respond. A short all-in below a full raise does not reopen raising for players who already acted, unless cumulative increases reach the required amount. If further betting is impossible, remaining community cards are dealt and the hand is settled."
msgstr ""

#: games/poker.rb:91
msgid "All-in puts in your remaining chips, subject to the betting limits. Other players still have to respond. If you cannot afford a full call, you may call with everything you have. An all-in smaller than a full raise does not normally let players who already acted raise again; several small increases must add up to a full raise before that right returns. If nobody can continue betting, the game completes the board where needed and compares the hands."
msgstr ""

#: games/categories.rb:187
msgid "Allow a shared victory"
msgstr "Povolit společné vítězství"

#: games/uno.rb:149
msgid "Allow challenging Wild Draw Four"
msgstr "Povolit zpochybnění karty Změna barvy a dobrat čtyři"

#: games/mexican_train.rb:114
msgid "Allow drawing even when having a playable piece is off by default. Enabling it lets you draw voluntarily before playing. You still get only one draw for the current decision, not repeated draws by pressing Space. After playing a double and gaining another decision, you may draw once again if needed. Drawing does not let you ignore an unfinished double."
msgstr ""

#: games/domino.rb:150
msgid "Allow drawing even when having a playable piece is on by default. Turn it off to require playing a tile you already hold whenever possible. Draw until finding a playable piece is separately off: when enabled, one Space draws a batch ending at the first newly drawn playable tile or an empty boneyard. It is still one drawing action, not many separate turns."
msgstr ""

#: games/makao.rb:137 games/uno.rb:152
msgid "Allow drawing with a playable card"
msgstr "Povolit dobrání i s hratelnou kartou v ruce"

#: games/uno.rb:100
msgid "Allow drawing with a playable card is on by default. Its separate limit is normally three voluntary cards per turn, from one to twenty. At the limit, another press only reports that you cannot draw; it does not secretly end the turn. If optional drawing is off, having a legal card prevents an ordinary draw."
msgstr ""

#: games/domino.rb:32 games/mexican_train.rb:14
msgid "Allow drawing with a playable tile"
msgstr "Povolit dobrání i s hratelným kamenem"

msgid "Allow drawing with a playable tile defaults to off. When enabled, one voluntary draw is permitted in the current decision; existing legal tiles remain playable even if the new one does not fit. It does not permit ignoring a required double. After playing a double you receive a new decision, with at most one new draw. Repeated Space without playing cannot draw repeatedly. There is no thinking-time setting or team mode."
msgstr ""

msgid "Allow drawing with a playable tile is on by default. Drawing never removes the right to play a legal tile already held. Without a legal move after drawing the turn ends. Forbid drawing disables both drawing options; an empty or forbidden boneyard and no legal tile cause an automatic pass."
msgstr ""

#: games/poker.rb:158
msgid "Allow exchanging all five cards"
msgstr "Povolit výměnu všech pěti karet"

#: games/reversi.rb:30
msgid "Allow passing even when a move exists"
msgstr "Povolit vynechání tahu, i když je možný tah"

#: games/reversi.rb:54
msgid "Allow passing is also enabled by default. It lets you give the turn to your opponent even when you have a legal move. You may do this repeatedly; voluntary passes alone do not produce a draw. Switch the option off if you want players to pass only when they cannot place a disc."
msgstr ""

msgid "Allow passing is on by default. P gives your turn to the opponent even if you can place a disc. There is no limit on voluntary passes and repeated passes do not end the game. When passing is disabled, a turn is skipped only if no placement is possible. A full board or no possible placement for either player ends the game: more discs wins, equal numbers draw. Old saved games retain their original rules."
msgstr ""

#: lib/game_surfaces/word_board.rb:72
msgid "Alphabetical rack order."
msgstr "Abecední pořadí ve stojánku."

#: games/scientific_war.rb:816
msgid "Already chosen: %{players}."
msgstr ""

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:75 lib/game_room_changelog.rb:97
msgid "Also added Biblios by dawidpieper (Pajper): a card game of building a library and bidding at auctions, for two to four players, with bots and Polish translation."
msgstr "Přidána také hra Biblios od autora dawidpieper (Pajper): karetní hra o budování knihovny a dražbách pro dva až čtyři hráče, s boty a polským překladem."

#: __app.rb:831 lib/game_shortcut_bindings.rb:60
msgid "Alt"
msgstr "Alt"

msgid "American / Atlantic City is the default. Each board changes field names and can change the layout, currency, starting capital, salary, building prices and bank supply. Larger boards have additional colour groups, up to six stations and four utilities. The details below describe the data actually used by this program, not a promise of identical economics in every published Monopoly edition."
msgstr ""

#: content/monopoly_boards.rb:10
msgid "American board / Atlantic City"
msgstr "Americká hrací deska / Atlantic City"

#: games/ninety_nine.rb:83
msgid "An ace gives you a choice of adding 1 or 11. A ten lets you add or subtract 10, but you cannot go below zero. The game asks for that choice before playing the card."
msgstr ""

#: games/tysiac.rb:92
msgid "An ace is worth 11, a ten 10, a king four, a queen three, a jack two and a nine zero. The cards total 120 points. Add any declared marriages before checking the bidder's contract."
msgstr ""

msgid "An empty hand wins the round for zero points. Other players add their remaining pips; double blank is always ten, even alongside other tiles. With an empty boneyard, a complete circuit without a legal play blocks the round and everyone scores their hand. Opening a train may create a move for an earlier player, so a pass counter alone does not end the round."
msgstr ""

#: games/ludo.rb:55
msgid "An exact roll is required to reach the finish"
msgstr "K dosažení cíle je nutné hodit přesné číslo"

#: games/ludo.rb:77
msgid "An exact roll is required to reach the finish is on by default. A pawn two squares from the finish needs a two: a larger result cannot move it. With this option off, an overshooting roll also takes the pawn to the finish."
msgstr ""

msgid "An exact roll is required to reach the finish: on by default. A roll going past the finish cannot move that pawn. When disabled, an excessive roll also brings it to the finish. Three consecutive sixes lose the turn: on by default; the third six ends the turn without moving a pawn for that roll, but does not undo previous moves."
msgstr ""

#: __app.rb:1810
msgid "An invitation to this table is already pending for this user."
msgstr "Tento uživatel už má nevyřízenou pozvánku k tomuto stolu."

#: games/krowa.rb:282
msgid "An observer does not take part in the game."
msgstr "Divák se hry neúčastní."

#: games/axel_pong.rb:277
msgid "An opponent who does not serve"
msgstr ""

#: games/uno.rb:99
msgid "An ordinary draw takes one card. If you still have no legal card afterwards, your turn ends automatically. Otherwise you may play. When the pile runs out, discards except the top card are shuffled back for drawing; nobody loses their hand."
msgstr ""

msgid "An uninterrupted line of at least four of your pieces horizontally, vertically or diagonally wins immediately. Filling all 42 fields without a winning line is a draw. This game has no configurable rule variants or board sizes. Both people and computers can play."
msgstr ""

#: games/monopoly.rb:62
msgid "An unowned street, station or utility may be bought when you land on it. The game gives its name, colour or type, and price. If you have enough cash, choose whether to buy. If you cannot afford it, the purchase is declined automatically. A property you do not buy remains available, unless the auction option sends it to auction."
msgstr ""

#: games/categories.rb:1329
msgid "Animal"
msgstr "Zvíře"

msgid "Announce lobby changes"
msgstr "Oznamovat změny v čekárně"

#: lib/game_room_screens.rb:193
msgid "Announce when a computer is added or removed"
msgstr "Oznamovat přidání nebo odebrání počítačového hráče"

#: lib/game_room_screens.rb:185
msgid "Announce when a player joins a table"
msgstr "Oznamovat připojení hráče ke stolu"

#: lib/game_room_screens.rb:189
msgid "Announce when a player leaves a table"
msgstr "Oznamovat odchod hráče od stolu"

#: lib/game_room_screens.rb:181
msgid "Announce when a table is created"
msgstr "Oznamovat vytvoření stolu"

#: lib/axel_pong/settings.rb:17
msgid "Announcer volume"
msgstr "Hlasitost komentátora"

#: games/krowa.rb:281
msgid "Another person is playing now."
msgstr "Teď hraje jiná osoba."

#: games/krowa.rb:285
msgid "Another word has already started."
msgstr "Již se začalo hrát jiné slovo."

#: games/categories.rb:129
msgid "Answer language"
msgstr "Jazyk odpovědí"

msgid "Answer language is Polish by default, with English also available. It chooses the alphabet used for drawing letters, not each player's interface language. Used letters are avoided until the selected alphabet has been exhausted. Category names are displayed in the player's interface language."
msgstr ""

#: games/categories.rb:94
msgid "Answer language is Polish by default; English is also available. It chooses the alphabet for letter draws and the language you agree to answer in, not the interface language. Category labels follow your interface. Letters do not repeat until the selected alphabet has been used up."
msgstr ""

msgid "Answer questions correctly to earn points. Speed does not affect the score, provided you answer before the time expires."
msgstr ""

