msgid "Rounding scores to units of five is on by default. With it, cards 2–9 are worth 5, and 10, jack, queen and king are worth 10. An ace before 2 is worth 5; a high ace or an ace in a set is worth 15. Without rounding, 2–9 use their printed values, face cards and 10 are worth 10, a low ace is worth 1 and a high or set ace 11. An ace left in your hand uses the high value."
msgstr ""

msgid "Rounding to five-point units is on by default: ranks two through nine are worth 5, ten and faces 10, a low ace 5, a high or set ace 15. With rounding off they are face value, faces 10, low ace 1 and high or set ace 11. An ace left in hand is always worth the high value. A hand joker is worth 20; a melded joker takes the represented value. An identity meld adds 10 per card."
msgstr ""

