msgid "The bid must be higher than the current one and within your reach."
msgstr "Nabídka musí být vyšší než aktuální a musíte si ji moci dovolit."

#: games/biblios.rb:354
msgid "The bid must be higher than the current one."
msgstr "Nabídka musí být vyšší než aktuální nabídka."

#: games/tysiac.rb:88
msgid "The bidder leads the first trick. Everyone plays one card, and the trick's winner leads next. A trick contains two cards with two players, or three cards with three. You must follow the first card's suit if possible. If you have none of that suit, you must use a trump if a trump suit has been established and you hold one. Only otherwise may you discard any card. You do not have to beat a higher card merely because you can."
msgstr ""

msgid "The bidder leads the first trick. Everyone plays one card, and the winner of those three cards leads next. You must follow the first card's suit if possible. If you have none of that suit, you must use a trump if a trump suit has been established and you hold one. Only otherwise may you discard any card. You do not have to beat a higher card merely because you can."
msgstr ""

#: games/poker.rb:178
msgid "The blind interval must be from 1 to 100."
msgstr "Interval zvyšování povinných sázek musí být od 1 do 100."

#: games/poker.rb:181
msgid "The blind multiplier must be from 2 to 10."
msgstr "Násobitel povinných sázek musí být od 2 do 10."

msgid "The board and the king"
msgstr ""

#: games/checkers.rb:121
msgid "The board can use numbered dark squares or chess-style coordinates. Numbered boards have 32, 50 or 72 playable squares, depending on size. Switching notation or rotating the view changes only how you inspect the board, not the rules or the other player's view."
msgstr ""

#: lib/game_surfaces/piece_board.rb:559
msgid "The board is rotated."
msgstr "Hrací deska je otočená."

#: games/checkers.rb:109
msgid "The board size may be 8 by 8, 10 by 10 or 12 by 12. These sizes give each side 12, 20 or 30 pieces respectively. Two rows in the middle begin empty. Changing the size does not automatically change the movement or capture rules, so check the other settings as well."
msgstr ""

#: lib/game_surfaces/piece_board.rb:559
msgid "The board uses its normal orientation."
msgstr "Deska je v obvyklé orientaci."

#: games/yahtzee.rb:69
msgid "The bonus for additional Yahtzees is enabled by default. First you must have written 50 in the Yahtzee row. Each later five-of-a-kind that you score in another row then adds 100 bonus points. A zero in Yahtzee does not unlock this bonus."
msgstr ""

#: games/monopoly.rb:74
msgid "The building and selling lists show the colour, existing buildings and cost or proceeds. Confirm an operation with Enter and stay in the list to continue managing properties. If no operation is possible, the game explains why instead of making you select a building you cannot buy."
msgstr ""

#: games/poker.rb:468
msgid "The call amount has changed to %{amount}. Choose your raise again."
msgstr "Částka k dorovnání se změnila na %{amount}. Vyberte navýšení znovu."

msgid "The cards are allocated one at a time, so you must decide where each card goes before the next is drawn. You must allocate precisely 1 card to the space in front of yourself and precisely 1 card to the Auction pile. The remaining cards go to the public space, which therefore always holds one card fewer than the number of players."
msgstr ""

#: games/biblios.rb:498
msgid "The cards are dealt and the Gift phase begins."
msgstr "Karty jsou rozdány a začíná fáze darů."

msgid "The categories are country, city, name, animal, plant and thing. Their labels follow each player's interface language, while the selected answer language determines the letters used in the match."
msgstr ""

#: games/quiz_party.rb:1315
msgid "The categories for the next round are being drawn."
msgstr "Losují se kategorie pro další kolo."

msgid "The chain and the first tile"
msgstr ""

msgid "The challenge failed. %{player} draws six cards."
msgstr "Zpochybnění neuspělo. %{player} dobírá šest karet."

msgid "The challenge succeeded. %{player} draws four cards."
msgstr "Zpochybnění bylo úspěšné. Hráč %{player} si dobírá čtyři karty."

#: games/tysiac.rb:85
msgid "The checkbox Set-aside cards go to the last trick winner is enabled by default. It awards the card points from both the unchosen talon and the bidder's discards to whoever takes the last trick, before checking the contract. Thus all 120 card points remain in play. It does not award marriages from those cards or add the cards to the winner's hand. If the checkbox is disabled, nobody scores those cards, so fewer than 120 card points may be available in tricks."
msgstr ""

#: games/scrabble_ui.rb:49
msgid "The chosen language decides which words count"
msgstr ""

#: games/uno.rb:103
msgid "The classic deck and drawing attacks"
msgstr ""

msgid "The classic game uses an 8 by 8 board and four discs in the centre. The first player uses black and moves first."
msgstr ""

#: games/battleship.rb:66
msgid "The computer places its own fleet automatically. It chooses shots using the same public answers available to a person, without seeing the opposing fleet. The shared bot-delay setting only adds a pause before its move; it does not change the rules or reveal extra information."
msgstr ""

#: games/mancala.rb:74
msgid "The computer uses the same rules and can see the whole board, just as you can. Calm uses a short search, Steady looks further and is the default, while Sharp considers more continuations and may need longer to answer. These settings change its planning effort, not the number of seeds or scoring."
msgstr ""

#: games/audio_ball.rb:190
msgid "The court is 25 steps long. By default, you hear your end on the right and the opponent's end on the left. An incoming ball travels from left to right; your shot travels from right to left. Headphones make it easier to follow the ball. You can reverse this listening perspective in your personal settings."
msgstr ""

#: games/battleship.rb:39 games/categories.rb:60 games/krowa.rb:36 games/quiz_party.rb:41 games/scientific_war.rb:91
msgid "The current game contains private data that cannot be transferred at this stage."
msgstr ""

#: games/ninety_nine.rb:80
msgid "The dealer changes between rounds, and the next active player starts. Seven or eight players use two decks. When the drawing pile runs out, discards are shuffled back in; this does not replace the cards people are holding. A new round deals new hands and resets the shared total, but token balances carry over."
msgstr ""

msgid "The dealer changes every round. The player to the dealer's left begins both bidding and the first trick. For team games, the table master may accept the alternating seat arrangement or assign every human and computer to a valid team before starting."
msgstr ""

#: lib/card_deck_history.rb:17
msgid "The deck was reshuffled."
msgstr "Balíček byl znovu zamíchán."

#: games/battleship.rb:54
msgid "The default Polish fleet has ten ships: one covering four squares, two covering three, three covering two, and four covering one. The other fleet has five ships, of lengths 5, 4, 3, 3 and 2. Both players always use the fleet chosen in the table settings."
msgstr ""

msgid "The default board is 8 by 8, with 12 pieces on each side. A 10 by 10 board gives each player 20 pieces; a 12 by 12 board gives 30. The two middle rows start empty. Size changes the space and starting army, not the selected movement rules."
msgstr ""

#: games/monopoly.rb:90
msgid "The default board is American / Atlantic City. A different board can change names, layout, currency, starting cash, Start salary and property economics. Larger boards also have more colour groups, stations and utilities. The profiles below are generated from the boards actually used by Game Room. Inspect individual deeds for purchase prices, rent levels and mortgage values."
msgstr ""

msgid "The default settings are the classic rules. The table creator may change entry, extra-roll, exact-finish, three-sixes and blockade rules."
msgstr ""

msgid "The default values are 1000 points to win, 30 points to bank a turn and 50 points for the first bank."
msgstr ""

msgid "The default variant deals two private cards to each player. There are four betting rounds: before the flop, after the three-card flop, after the one-card turn, and after the one-card river. The five table cards are shared. At showdown choose the best five cards from the seven available: both, one or neither of your private cards may be used. The game announces each stage and newly exposed table cards."
msgstr ""

#: games/base.rb:339
msgid "The delay belongs to the table and is preserved when a supported game is saved. It does not prevent permitted human actions while waiting. Near a turn deadline the wait is shortened so it cannot keep the bot from acting in time."
msgstr "Prodleva je nastavením stolu a při uložení podporované hry se zachová. Během čekání nebrání povoleným akcím lidských hráčů. Blíží-li se konec časového limitu tahu, čekání se zkrátí, aby bot mohl včas provést tah."

#: games/taboo_ui.rb:85
msgid "The describer presses Enter when everyone is ready. After three seconds of preparation, a sound starts the clock and the card appears. Enter marks a correct guess; P skips the card. An opponent presses B to report a violation. Each decision immediately brings the next card, but never restarts the clock. Reading and thinking use the same time as speaking."
msgstr ""

msgid "The describing player presses Enter when everyone is ready. After three seconds, a sound starts the turn and reveals the card. Enter marks a correct guess; P skips. An opponent presses B for a violation. The next card appears immediately without restarting the clock. Guessers do not press anything. The deck is shuffled; no card repeats until exhaustion, and reshuffling avoids an immediate repeat."
msgstr ""

#: games/cat_head_tail.rb:403 games/ludo.rb:276 games/yahtzee.rb:518 lib/game_surfaces/roll_and_score.rb:177
msgid "The dice have not been rolled."
msgstr "Kostkami se ještě neházelo."

#: games/cat_head_tail.rb:403
msgctxt "cat_head_tail"
msgid "The dice have not been rolled."
msgstr "Kostkami se ještě neházelo."

msgid "The die has not been rolled"
msgstr "Kostkou se ještě neházelo"

#: games/audio_ball.rb:184
msgid "The difficulty level determines the starting ball speed and how much it increases during a rally. The times below describe a full flight across the 25-step court after a serve."
msgstr ""

#: games/rummy_ui.rb:196 games/rummy_ui.rb:74
msgid "The discard pile is empty."
msgstr "Odhazovací balíček je prázdný."

#: games/uno.rb:178
msgid "The draw limit must be from 1 to 20."
msgstr "Limit dobírání musí být od 1 do 20."

msgid "The easy pool contains country, city, name, animal, plant, thing, profession, food and colour. Medium adds surname, famous person, sport, vehicle, clothing, body part, building, musical instrument and book. Hard also adds film, song, music group, river, mountain, island, language, invention and chemical element."
msgstr ""

#: games/rummy_ui.rb:141
msgid "The elimination limit defaults to 500. Check it after settling the whole round: reaching or exceeding it eliminates a player. If everyone would go out together, the lowest total wins, with a shared result for equal lowest scores. Normally the last player below the limit wins. A blocked round simply charges each remaining hand, without a rummy multiplier. Penalties, including 300 for an unreturned table card, add points in this mode rather than subtracting them."
msgstr ""

msgid "The elimination score limit defaults to 500. Players reaching it leave after the round, not in the middle of a turn. The last remaining player wins. If everyone crosses the limit together, the lowest total wins; a tie for that lowest total is a shared victory."
msgstr ""

msgid "The final bidder takes the publicly revealed talon, then gives one card to each opponent. The bidder may keep the winning contract or raise it, in steps of 5, up to 400. The bidder leads the first trick; every later trick is led by the winner of the previous one."
msgstr ""

#: games/categories.rb:1418
msgid "The final cycle ends after round %{round}."
msgstr "Závěrečný cyklus skončí po kole %{round}."

#: games/farkle.rb:52
msgid "The first bank has its own minimum, normally 50 points. Until you have a positive saved score, you must collect at least that much in a single turn to bank. Later turns use the ordinary banking minimum, normally 30. Both settings can be changed at the table."
msgstr ""

#: games/makao.rb:480
msgid "The first card in the packet cannot begin this move."
msgstr "První kartou ve skupině nelze zahájit tento tah."

#: games/makao.rb:500
msgid "The first card in the packet does not defend against the draw penalty."
msgstr "První karta ve skupině neodvrací trestné dobírání."

#: games/makao.rb:501
msgid "The first card in the packet does not defend against the waiting penalty."
msgstr "První karta ve skupině neodvrací trest vynechání tahu."

#: games/makao.rb:502
msgid "The first card in the packet does not satisfy the requested rank."
msgstr "První karta ve skupině nemá požadovanou hodnotu."

#: games/spades.rb:217
msgid "The first card of a trick sets its suit. You must follow that suit if you can. Game Room has one exception: if the ace is your only spade, you may keep it when spades are led and play another suit instead. When you cannot follow suit, you may play any card; you are not forced to use a trump."
msgstr ""

msgid "The first card sets the led suit. You must follow that suit when possible, except that you may withhold the ace of spades when it is your only spade. Otherwise you may play any card, including a spade. The highest spade wins the trick; if no spade was played, the highest card of the led suit wins. Aces are high and 2s are low."
msgstr ""

msgid "The first empty hand wins the round for zero points. Others count their remaining pips. Double blank is ten points only when it is the player's sole remaining tile; otherwise it is zero. A full circuit with no legal placement and no available drawing blocks the round and everyone scores their hand. Deliberate timeouts alone cannot prove a block."
msgstr ""

#: games/rummy.rb:59
msgid "The first meld minimum must be from 15 to 90."
msgstr "Minimální hodnota prvního vyložení musí být od 15 do 90."

msgid "The first player in each team has steps, serves and returns pitched three semitones lower than their partner. For teams A and B against C and D, A and C have the lower sound, while B and D keep the standard pitch. Everyone hears the same distinction, including spectators after changing perspective. Simultaneous paddle sounds do not cut each other off."
msgstr "Kroky, podání a odrazy prvního hráče v každém týmu znějí o tři půltóny níže než u jeho spoluhráče. Hrají-li A a B proti C a D, mají A a C nižší zvuk, zatímco B a D si zachovávají standardní výšku. Všichni slyší stejné rozlišení, včetně pozorovatelů po změně perspektivy. Současně znějící zvuky pálek se navzájem nepřerušují."

#: games/axel_pong.rb:262
msgid "The first player in each team uses a different footstep recording, while their partner keeps the standard footsteps. For teams A and B against C and D, A and C use the new sound; B and D keep the usual sound. Footstep pitch still indicates paddle position, without an extra pitch shift for either partner. Serves and returns by A and C are pitched four semitones lower than those by B and D. Everyone hears the same distinction, including spectators after changing perspective. Simultaneous paddle sounds do not cut each other off."
msgstr ""

msgid "The first player to place all four pawns at the finish wins."
msgstr ""

msgid "The first player to place all four pawns on the final home field wins."
msgstr ""

msgid "The first player to play the last card wins the game."
msgstr ""

msgid "The first player whose banked total reaches or exceeds the selected score limit wins immediately."
msgstr ""

#: games/mexican_train.rb:120
msgid "The first player with an empty hand wins the round and receives zero points. Everyone else adds the numbers on their remaining tiles. The 0/0 always counts as 10 here, even alongside other tiles. If the boneyard is empty and nobody can make a legal play over a complete circuit, the round is blocked and all players count their hands. Opening a train may create a new legal move, so merely counting passes is not enough to declare a block."
msgstr ""

#: games/checkers.rb:945 games/chess.rb:850
msgid "The first player's pieces are at the bottom."
msgstr "Figury prvního hráče jsou dole."

#: games/categories.rb:1368 games/categories.rb:1382 games/quiz_party.rb:1259 games/quiz_party.rb:1289
msgid "The first round is being prepared."
msgstr "Připravuje se první kolo."

msgid "The first seat serves first. Service changes after every two completed points. The table selects a target of 7, 11 or 21 points, but a player also needs a lead of at least two. At 10–10 in an 11-point match, for example, 11–10 is not enough; 12–10 wins. There is a short break after each point before the next serve."
msgstr ""

#: games/axel_pong.rb:259
msgid "The first serve becomes available once the players are connected and ready, without an extra countdown. In a human-only match, you hear the variant, difficulty and target, then who serves. The break after subsequent points remains as described above."
msgstr ""

msgid "The first serve of a human match becomes available after both sides are ready and a three-second countdown. You hear the variant, difficulty and target, then who serves. A bot match starts without this countdown. This does not change the break after subsequent points."
msgstr ""

msgid "The first server is chosen at random once for the match, also against a bot. Service changes after every two completed points. This two-point sequence continues between sets and at deuce; it never changes to one serve each."
msgstr ""

msgid "The first server is chosen at the start of a human match; against a bot, the human starts. Service changes after every two completed points. Choose a target of 7, 11 or 21, with a lead of at least two points required to win. At 10–10 in an 11-point match, 11–10 is not enough; 12–10 wins. After a point there is a three-second break for the goal recording, followed by the score and a further 2.7-second serve delay. You can reposition your paddle during this pause, but serving requires a new press after it ends."
msgstr ""

#: games/audio_ball.rb:208
msgid "The first server is drawn at random once at the start of the match, whether you play a person or a bot. Service then changes after every two completed points. This sequence continues across sets and during play for a two-point lead. A new set does not restart it, and there is no switch to one serve each at deuce."
msgstr ""

msgid "The first starting player is drawn; subsequent starters rotate among remaining players. Each player has a personal train, initially closed, and everyone shares the permanently public Mexican train. A tile must match the end of an accessible train, or the station for an empty train. You may play on your own train, the Mexican train or another open train. Playing on your own closes it; playing on someone else's does not close theirs or yours."
msgstr ""

#: games/scrabble.rb:123
msgid "The first word must cover H8."
msgstr "První slovo musí procházet polem H8."

#: games/battleship.rb:711
msgid "The fleet is ready."
msgstr "Flotila je připravena."

#: games/battleship.rb:656
msgid "The fleet is ready. Do you want to seal it?"
msgstr "Flotila je připravena. Chcete potvrdit její rozmístění?"

#: games/battleship.rb:608
msgid "The fleets are being placed."
msgstr "Probíhá rozmísťování flotil."

#: games/quiz_party.rb:88
msgid "The full Witcher set combines its two subject collections. Witcher — games contains game-related questions; Witcher — books and adaptations contains books and screen adaptations. Choose the full set for a mixture or the narrower set for that medium. The accepted answer comes from the chosen question data, not a live search or a judge's decision during play."
msgstr ""

#: games/krowa_support/presentation.rb:33
msgid "The gallery remembers the words you have guessed on your own and your best attempt count for each one. You can open it before a game or after it ends. Its menu lets you sort by date, attempt count or word length. Select a word with Enter to open its leaderboard. After a game, you can agree to publish your result, which also opens the leaderboard for that word."
msgstr ""

#: games/krowa_support/presentation.rb:34
msgid "The gallery remembers words you solved in solo play and your best attempt count for each. You can open it before, during or after a game. Its context menu sorts by newest, attempts or length; selecting a word opens its leaderboard. After finishing a game you can choose to publish a result. Publication is optional, and unavailable rankings do not prevent Random word, Race or Word Tower from being played."
msgstr ""

#: games/tysiac.rb:98
msgid "The game announces when someone goes onto the barrel and records it in the history. S reads scores and marks the players currently on the barrel. Shift+S also tells you how many barrel chances they have left."
msgstr ""

#: __app.rb:2745
msgid "The game cannot start until these players join the real-time session: %{players}."
msgstr "Hru nelze zahájit, dokud se tito hráči nepřipojí k relaci v reálném čase: %{players}."

#: lib/game_screen.rb:1397 lib/game_screen.rb:1430 lib/game_screen.rb:2177
msgid "The game changed before your action was accepted. Please choose again."
msgstr "Stav hry se změnil, než byla vaše akce přijata. Vyberte prosím znovu."

msgid "The game could not be opened. Please try again."
msgstr "Hru se nepodařilo otevřít. Zkuste to prosím znovu."

#: __app.rb:1011
msgid "The game could not be saved. The table was not closed by this operation."
msgstr "Hru se nepodařilo uložit. Tato operace stůl nezavřela."

msgid "The game deals five cards by default. In the joker profile it uses two jokers, and the first table card cannot be a two, three, four, ace, attacking king or joker."
msgstr ""

#: games/three_five_eight.rb:433
msgid "The game ended in a draw between %{players}."
msgstr ""

#: games/base.rb:1075 games/base.rb:1479 games/chess.rb:431
msgid "The game ended in a draw."
msgstr "Hra skončila remízou."

#: games/categories.rb:1052
msgid "The game ended with a shared victory: %{players}."
msgstr "Hra skončila společným vítězstvím: %{players}."

#: games/mancala.rb:72
msgid "The game ends as soon as either row is empty. The other player moves all seeds remaining in their row into their own store. The larger store wins; equal stores mean a draw. There is no requirement to feed an empty opponent in Kalah."
msgstr ""

msgid "The game ends as soon as one player completes a row, column or diagonal of three marks. If all nine fields are occupied without such a line, the game ends in a draw."
msgstr ""

msgid "The game ends immediately when a move completes a line of four pieces. If all 42 fields are occupied and nobody has four in a row, the game ends in a draw."
msgstr ""

#: games/scrabble_ui.rb:62
msgid "The game ends when someone empties their rack and the bag is empty. It also ends as blocked when exchanging is unavailable and three complete circuits pass without a tile being placed. A legal word worth zero still breaks this sequence. At the end, subtract each player's remaining tile values. If a player went out, they also gain the other players' remaining values; a blocked game has no such bonus. Blanks are worth zero. The highest adjusted score wins, with a shared result if tied."
msgstr ""

#: games/reversi.rb:55
msgid "The game ends when the board is full or neither player has a legal placement under the selected rules. The player with more discs wins; equal numbers mean a draw. Having no move yourself does not end the game if your opponent can still play."
msgstr ""

#: games/base.rb:998
msgid "The game has already ended."
msgstr "Hra již skončila."

#: __app.rb:1007
msgid "The game has been saved."
msgstr "Partie byla uložena."

#: games/board_game.rb:230
msgid "The game has ended. You can still inspect the board."
msgstr "Hra skončila. Herní desku si můžete dál prohlížet."

msgid "The game includes the agreed international board list and a Polish board. Every board uses the same rules engine and differs only in names and presentation."
msgstr ""

#: games/base.rb:1371 games/ludo.rb:284 games/ninety_nine.rb:944 games/scientific_war.rb:825
msgid "The game is finished."
msgstr "Hra skončila."

#: games/spades.rb:2599
msgid "The game is finished. %{winner} won."
msgstr "Hra skončila. Vítěz: %{winner}."

msgid "The game is split into two phases. During the Gift phase players receive free cards. During the Auction phase players purchase cards in an auction."
msgstr ""

msgid "The game uses the standard 8 by 8 chessboard and the orthodox initial position. White moves first."
msgstr ""

msgid "The goal"
msgstr ""

#: games/makao.rb:171
msgid "The hand size must be from 3 to 15."
msgstr "Počet karet v ruce musí být od 3 do 15."

#: games/war.rb:36
msgid "The highest card wins the battle and takes all the cards from the table. Aces are highest, then kings, queens, jacks, tens and so on down to the lowest card in the deck. Suits do not matter. The cards taken go to the bottom of the winner's pile in random order."
msgstr ""

#: games/spades.rb:218
msgid "The highest spade wins. If nobody played a spade, the highest card of the led suit wins. A high card in another suit does not win merely because it is high. For example, an ace of hearts cannot beat a low club in a club-led trick unless hearts were the led suit instead."
msgstr ""

#: games/krowa_support/presentation.rb:36
msgid "The host can save Race or Word Tower after the current word is ready and all submitted attempts have been checked. The local save includes the private solution and can be resumed with the same players in a new table. The table closes only after the save is verified. Daily Krowa and Random word cannot be saved for later."
msgstr ""

#: games/krowa.rb:489
msgid "The host changes the word. Race attempts and time start over."
msgstr "Hostitel stolu mění slovo. Pokusy i čas závodu se počítají znovu od začátku."

#: games/krowa_support/presentation.rb:16
msgid "The host must remain at the table: their client checks attempts while keeping the solution in local hidden storage."
msgstr ""

#: games/krowa_support/presentation.rb:14
msgid "The host selects the table variant. Daily Krowa and Random word can be started alone; Race and Word Tower require at least two players. A table holds up to eight players."
msgstr ""

msgid "The host's local secret is missing. Return to the computer where the game was started."
msgstr "Chybí místní tajný údaj hostitele stolu. Vraťte se k počítači, na kterém byla hra zahájena."

#: games/ninety_nine.rb:85
msgid "The important totals: 33, 66 and 99"
msgstr ""

#: games/base.rb:1286
msgid "The installed game content pack does not match the table."
msgstr "Nainstalovaný balíček herního obsahu neodpovídá balíčku tohoto stolu."

#: games/base.rb:1283
msgid "The installed game content pack has a different version."
msgstr "Nainstalovaný balíček herního obsahu má jinou verzi."

msgid "The international editions use 40 or 60 squares, different currencies and starting cash. The larger boards include additional colour groups, six stations and four utilities. The Polish board is a custom Game Room edition. Some economic details and event cards are Game Room adaptations, not verified copies of QC editions."
msgstr ""

msgid "The invalid-word setting offers six policies: correct or end the turn, each with no penalty, minus 5 or minus 10 points. The default is correction without penalty. One submitted attempt incurs at most one penalty, regardless of the number of invalid words. Invalid words return all draft tiles to the rack and do not consume bonuses. Geometry errors have no penalty. Preview calculates points but never checks the dictionary."
msgstr ""

#: games/scientific_war.rb:537
msgid "The jacks cancel each other out; the card order does not change."
msgstr ""

#: games/scientific_war.rb:553
msgid "The joker cancels the war: %{player} wins the trick and takes %{count} card."
msgid_plural "The joker cancels the war: %{player} wins the trick and takes %{count} cards."
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: games/scientific_war.rb:557
msgid "The joker forces a war. %{count} card stays on the table for the next trick."
msgid_plural "The joker forces a war. %{count} cards stay on the table for the next trick."
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: games/scientific_war.rb:543
msgid "The jokers cancel each other out."
msgstr ""

#: games/categories.rb:366 games/categories.rb:387
msgid "The judge finished reviewing the answers."
msgstr "Rozhodčí dokončil hodnocení odpovědí."

msgid "The judge started reviewing the answers."
msgstr "Rozhodčí začal hodnotit odpovědi."

msgid "The judge, not the program, decides whether an answer is correct and whether answers should be treated as duplicates. The judge's decision is final."
msgstr ""

#: games/chess.rb:50
msgid "The king is what you are protecting"
msgstr ""

msgid "The king moves one field in any direction. The queen moves any distance along a row, column or diagonal. A rook moves along rows and columns; a bishop along diagonals. These pieces cannot jump over occupied fields. A knight jumps in an L: two fields along one axis and one along the other, regardless of intervening pieces."
msgstr ""

#: games/three_five_eight.rb:741
msgid "The kitty is %{cards}."
msgstr ""

#: games/chess.rb:55
msgid "The knight moves in an L: two squares along a row or column, then one square sideways. It can jump over pieces in between. The king normally moves one square in any direction, but never onto a square attacked by the opponent. Two kings therefore cannot stand next to each other."
msgstr ""

#: games/scientific_war.rb:59
msgid "The last player who still has cards wins. The table has a trick limit from 20 to 100, 50 by default. When it is reached, the player with the most cards wins; if several players have the same highest number, the game is a draw. A very long game with many players may end a little earlier in the same way, because a table can store only a limited number of moves."
msgstr ""

#: games/battleship.rb:661
msgid "The last ship was taken back."
msgstr "Umístění poslední lodi bylo vráceno zpět."

#: games/scrabble_ui.rb:60
msgid "The last tiles and the final score"
msgstr ""

#: games/categories.rb:1030
msgid "The lead is tied. A tie-break will be played only by %{players}; the judge will be selected from the other participants."
msgstr "Na prvním místě je remíza. Rozhodujícího kola se zúčastní pouze tito hráči: %{players}; rozhodčí bude vybrán z ostatních účastníků."

msgid "The lead is tied. Another complete judge cycle will be played."
msgstr "Na prvním místě je remíza. Odehraje se další úplný cyklus rozhodčích."

#: games/quiz_party.rb:901
msgid "The lead is tied. Another round will be played: %{players}."
msgstr "Na prvním místě je remíza. Odehraje se další kolo: %{players}."

#: games/spades.rb:2647
msgid "The led suit is %{suit}."
msgstr "Vynesená barva je %{suit}."

#: __app.rb:925
msgid "The local saved game is no longer available."
msgstr "Místně uložená hra již není dostupná."

#: games/checkers.rb:283
msgid "The longest capture is mandatory. This piece cannot begin the required sequence. Choose: %{fields}."
msgstr "Je povinné provést nejdelší braní. Tímto kamenem nelze zahájit požadovanou posloupnost. Vyberte: %{fields}."

msgid "The main field contains Roll the dice, or a decision required by the square. A completed turn advances automatically. Property management and trades remain available through their shortcuts."
msgstr "Hlavní pole obsahuje volbu Hodit kostkami nebo rozhodnutí vyžadované polem hrací desky. Po dokončení tahu hra automaticky pokračuje dalším tahem. Správa nemovitostí a výměny zůstávají dostupné prostřednictvím svých zkratek."

msgid "The main list contains only actions that make sense in the current situation. Roll, buy or decline property, manage buildings and mortgages, trade, resolve debt and leave jail from the same shared game screen."
msgstr "Hlavní seznam obsahuje pouze akce, které dávají v aktuální situaci smysl. Na stejné společné herní obrazovce můžete házet kostkami, kupovat nebo odmítat nemovitosti, spravovat budovy a zástavy, vyměňovat, řešit dluhy a opouštět vězení."

#: games/krowa_support/presentation.rb:35
msgid "The main menu's Leaderboards entry gives access to Krowa word results and Word Tower results, including round details. Your gallery and custom dictionary are local and separate for each account. To remove custom words, open My dictionary in Krowa settings, select them with Space and use Remove selected. Removing a word does not rewrite attempts already made in a game."
msgstr ""

msgid "The match ends after the round in which at least one player reaches the target score. The highest score wins."
msgstr ""

#: games/farkle.rb:179
msgid "The minimum entry score cannot be negative."
msgstr "Minimální počet bodů pro vstup do hry nesmí být záporný."

#: games/farkle.rb:178
msgid "The minimum turn score cannot be negative."
msgstr "Minimální počet bodů za tah nesmí být záporný."

#: games/checkers.rb:71
msgid "The move capturing the most pieces is mandatory"
msgstr "Je povinný tah, který bere nejvíce kamenů"

msgid "The move capturing the most pieces is mandatory is on by default. Compare complete capture paths for all your pieces, not just the first jump, and choose one taking the greatest number. This option requires mandatory capture and completing capture sequences."
msgstr ""

#: games/quiz_party.rb:1313
msgid "The next question is being prepared."
msgstr "Připravuje se další otázka."

#: games/categories.rb:209
msgid "The number of categories shown in a round cannot exceed the size of the selected pool."
msgstr "Počet kategorií zobrazených v jednom kole nesmí překročit počet kategorií ve vybrané sadě."

#: games/categories.rb:206
msgid "The number of categories shown in a round must be between 1 and 9."
msgstr "Počet kategorií zobrazených v jednom kole musí být od 1 do 9."

#: games/yahtzee.rb:111
msgid "The number of matches must be from 1 to 10."
msgstr "Počet partií musí být od 1 do 10."

msgid "The number of starting tokens is configurable and defaults to 9. Omniscient bots is an optional challenge mode in which computers can see every player's current hand while planning; it is deliberately unfair and is off by default. Ordinary bots infer hidden cards from their own hand and public play."
msgstr ""

#: games/ninety_nine.rb:195
msgid "The number of starting tokens must be greater than zero."
msgstr "Počáteční počet žetonů musí být větší než nula."

#: __app.rb:1808 __app.rb:2526 lib/game_room_widget.rb:159 lib/game_screen.rb:2225
msgid "The operation could not be completed. Please try again."
msgstr "Operaci se nepodařilo dokončit. Zkuste to prosím znovu."

#: games/checkers.rb:404
msgid "The opponent has no kings."
msgstr "Soupeř nemá žádné dámy."

#: games/checkers.rb:957 games/chess.rb:862
msgid "The opponent's pieces are at the bottom."
msgstr "Soupeřovy figury jsou dole."

#: games/poker.rb:87
msgid "The optional Jacks or better rule restricts opening the first betting round: you need at least a pair of jacks or a stronger combination, such as two pairs. Once someone has opened, a weaker hand may call. This restriction does not apply to the second betting round. Both this option and exchanging all five cards are off by default."
msgstr ""

#: games/tysiac.rb:89
msgid "The order from strongest to weakest is ace, ten, king, queen, jack, nine. A trump beats every non-trump. With no trump in the trick, the highest card of the led suit wins. At the beginning of the deal there is no trump suit."
msgstr ""

#: games/domino.rb:147
msgid "The other choices are Double 12 (91 tiles), 2× Double 9 (110), 2× Double 12 (182), 4× Double 6 (112), 4× Double 9 (220), 4× Double 12 (364), Double 15 (136) and Double 18 (190). The number after Double is the largest number on a tile; 2× or 4× means two or four copies of the complete set. Undealt tiles form the boneyard, the face-down draw pile."
msgstr ""

#: games/mancala.rb:568
msgid "The other row: %{values}."
msgstr "Druhý řádek: %{values}."

#: games/chess.rb:232
msgid "The path from %{from} to %{to} is blocked."
msgstr "Cesta z pole %{from} na %{to} je zablokovaná."

#: games/chess.rb:251
msgid "The pawn cannot move from %{from} to %{to} in this position."
msgstr "Pěšec se v této pozici nemůže přesunout z pole %{from} na %{to}."

#: lib/game_room_presence_screen.rb:43
msgid "The people count is the sum of room membership counts: it includes observers and excludes bots. A person in more than one room may be counted more than once. This is not a global online count."
msgstr ""

msgid "The pile total is %{total}."
msgstr "Součet hodnot na hromádce je %{total}."

#: games/tysiac.rb:79
msgid "The player after the dealer opens at no less than 100. Later bids rise in steps of five. Passing removes you from this auction, not from the game. You may bid up to 120 plus the values of the marriages you currently hold, with an overall maximum of 400. A marriage is a king and queen of the same suit."
msgstr ""

msgid "The player after the dealer opens the auction and must bid at least 100. Later bids increase in steps of 5. A player who passes cannot bid again in that deal, and a player may not bid above 120 without holding at least one marriage."
msgstr ""

msgid "The player after the dealer opens the auction and must bid at least 100. Later bids increase in steps of 5. A player who passes cannot bid again in that deal. The maximum declaration is 120 plus the value of every marriage currently held, up to 400."
msgstr ""

#: games/domino.rb:144
msgid "The player holding the highest dealt double starts. A double is a tile with equal numbers, such as 6/6. If no hand has a double, the highest total decides; ties use the round's rotating priority. The starter may play any tile, not necessarily the double that gave them the start. A normal round ends as soon as someone uses their last tile."
msgstr ""

#: games/domino.rb:153
msgid "The player who empties their hand scores zero. Others add the numbers on their remaining tiles. For instance, 3/5 is worth 8. The 0/0 is a special case: it is worth 10 if it is the only tile left in your hand, but zero if you also have other tiles. If a whole circuit passes with no possible play and no usable draw pile, the round is blocked and everyone counts their remaining hand."
msgstr ""

msgid "The player with more discs wins. Equal totals are a draw."
msgstr ""

#: games/scientific_war.rb:47
msgid "The player with the strongest card wins the trick and puts all its cards on their pile. Normally the ace is the strongest card and the two the weakest. Suits do not matter."
msgstr ""

msgid "The players then add the numbers on their dice, and the player with the most Victory Points wins. The numbers on the cards are not Victory Points; they only determine who wins each category."
msgstr ""

msgid "The players' starting fields, in seating order, are 1, 14, 27 and 40 on the same shared track."
msgstr ""

msgid "The playing area is 25 steps wide. By default, each player hears their own end on the right and the opponent's end on the left. You can reverse your listening perspective in the personal settings without changing the opponent's sound."
msgstr ""

msgid "The playing area is 25 steps wide. Each player hears their own end on the right and the opponent's end on the left. This listening perspective is the same for both players: your own end is always on the right."
msgstr ""

#: games/rummy.rb:162
msgid "The prepared melds do not reach the first meld minimum."
msgstr "Připravené kombinace nedosahují minima pro první vyložení."

#: games/biblios.rb:1102
msgid "The public space is empty"
msgstr "Společná nabídka je prázdná"

#: games/biblios.rb:1290
